{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/base/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:15:47.944726Z","id":"94f64dc940ff620c43e5ada05050870591c70a23e2a4c79e9d8282d31f8bb0c6","body":{"detail":"No kubectl, kustomize or cluster was available: deploy/k8s/{base,sqlite,postgres,postgres-dev} were never built with kustomize nor applied. clax-fleet's tests check only that the variables they set are ones the binary reads and that base/fleet.toml parses (crates/clax-fleet/src/main.rs tests). Validate with `kubectl kustomize deploy/k8s/<overlay> | kubeconform -strict` and a kind cluster.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"0c4b6e894d7aeafe5e37ff904a514eccbed1c194ff49f260ce9959745c015733"},"summary":"The manifests have not been rendered or validated against a cluster","tags":["test-coverage","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/base/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:35:33.800789Z","id":"f3620c4abb15438a738985bb05d5c9099f1fa32a754d02ce800226f4011f286a","body":{"detail":"Port 7480 takes x-clax-fleet-hop and x-clax-fleet-instance from any caller (crates/clax-fleet/src/fleet.rs dispatch, open record 462bbaa8) and carries session cookies and tokens in plaintext between pods (proxy.rs forward); port 7481 serves /status with every tenant's instance name without authentication (fleet.rs admin_router). With no NetworkPolicy in base, sqlite or postgres, any pod in any namespace of the cluster can reach both, and in postgres-dev any pod can log into the database with the password committed in deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/kustomization.yaml. A NetworkPolicy is the cheapest layer that turns the hop headers' trust into 'only the Ingress controller and the fleet's own pods'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"bdd2376fb58a77fe70d4e2847620b4c3435002a6f0cf9c36a26755f4005923a3"},"suggested_fix":"Add a NetworkPolicy to base allowing ingress to 7480 only from the fleet's pods and the Ingress controller's namespace (a label the operator sets), and to 7481 only from the fleet's pods (kubelet probes are not subject to it on most CNIs); add one to postgres-dev allowing 5432 only from the fleet's pods.","summary":"No NetworkPolicy limits who reaches the pods' 7480 and 7481 ports","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","security","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/base/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:36:07.215088Z","id":"5f8050199e39712a60422168a0250029cf65810daf82304e2444bd2199ef391f","body":{"detail":"docs/kubernetes.md:60-61 says base/fleet.toml becomes the clax-fleet-catalog ConfigMap, and docs/kubernetes.md:50-53 already tells operators to keep an overlay of their own for the image. An operator's catalog belongs in that overlay too, which kustomize supports with a configMapGenerator entry of the same name and `behavior: replace` (https://kubectl.docs.kubernetes.io/references/kustomize/kustomization/configmapgenerator/), keeping disableNameSuffixHash so pods are not restarted. Without it, upgrading the repository conflicts with local edits to base files.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":16},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"ac2002d7df93bb7591c0f98bbe0ba13bfdd5bd250b7bfb2d1f38bbec1d99d73a"},"suggested_fix":"Add to docs/kubernetes.md an example overlay (resources: [github.com/empathic/clax//deploy/k8s/postgres?ref=<tag>], images:, configMapGenerator: [{name: clax-fleet-catalog, behavior: replace, files: [fleet.toml], options: {disableNameSuffixHash: true}}]) and present it as the way to deploy.","summary":"Supplying one's own catalog means editing deploy/k8s/base/fleet.toml in the repository; the docs show no overlay that replaces it","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","devops","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/base/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:15.293897Z","id":"cf33fc4f624fa0e7152c34099d471abb33482baa831634ce4ec3e6d16fb79e32","body":{"detail":"deploy/k8s/base/kustomization.yaml:12-15 lists serviceaccount, service and pdb only; grep -rln NetworkPolicy deploy docs matches only deploy/k8s/base/.qual. crates/clax-fleet/src/fleet.rs dispatch (~754-769) picks the instance from x-clax-fleet-instance whenever the hop header is >0; admin_router (fleet.rs:715-742) serves /status with no auth; deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/kustomization.yaml:19 commits POSTGRES_PASSWORD=clax-dev.","kind":"comment","references":"f3620c4abb15438a738985bb05d5c9099f1fa32a754d02ce800226f4011f286a","summary":"confirmed: no NetworkPolicy exists in any overlay","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/base/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:41:21.162997Z","id":"1424e4aa8feca5fd6fca6589ec822f69dc4cc306fc4054b7b8476bb48362609c","body":{"detail":"deploy/k8s/base/kustomization.yaml:16-24 generates clax-fleet-catalog from base/fleet.toml with disableNameSuffixHash. docs/kubernetes.md:50-53 recommends an overlay of one's own for the image, and 60-61 says base/fleet.toml becomes the ConfigMap, with no example of replacing it. kustomize supports behavior: replace on a generator of the same name (https://kubectl.docs.kubernetes.io/references/kustomize/kustomization/configmapgenerator/). Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"5f8050199e39712a60422168a0250029cf65810daf82304e2444bd2199ef391f","summary":"confirmed: the catalog lives in base/fleet.toml with no documented overlay to replace it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
